  doi          = {10.1172/JCI130808},
  abstract     = {A single subanesthetic dose of ketamine, an NMDA receptor
                  (NMDAR) antagonist, produces rapid and sustained
                  antidepressant actions in depressed patients, addressing a
                  major unmet need for the treatment of mood disorders. Ketamine
                  produces a rapid increase in extracellular glutamate and
                  synaptic formation in the prefrontal cortex, but the initial
