  doi          = {10.48550/arXiv.2403.11207},
  abstract     = {Reconstructions of visual perception from brain activity have
                  improved tremendously, but the practical utility of such
                  methods has been limited. This is because such models are
                  trained independently per subject where each subject requires
                  dozens of hours of expensive fMRI training data to attain
                  high-quality results. The present work showcases high-quality
