                  correction of action and, by extension, the interpretation of
                  the behavior of others. It is hypothesized that the neural
                  substrate for these processes during motivational and
                  affective behavior lies within the interactions of anterior
                  cingulate, insula, and orbitofrontal cortices. Generation of
                  visceral autonomic correlates of control reinforce
                  experiential engagement in simulatory models and underpin
                  concepts such as somatic markers to bridge the dualistic
                  divide.},
  urldate      = {2026-05-26},
