                  architecture, produce the same type of relationship observed
                  by Gu et al. between the average/modal controllability and
                  weighted degree. Finally, we find that resting state networks
                  defined with fMRI cannot be attributed specific control roles.
                  In summary, our study highlights some warning and caveats in
                  the brain controllability framework.},
  urldate      = {2026-05-25},
  keywords     = {Brain controllability; Brain networks; Complex networks; Null
