                  critical frequency is approximately 10 Hz. For excitatory
                  networks and networks with randomly distributed excitatory and
                  inhibitory connections, time delays and non-zero dendritic
                  time constants have no impact on network stability but do
                  effect dispersion frequencies. Random networks with both
                  excitatory and inhibitory connections can have multiple
                  marginally stable modes at low delta frequencies.},
