  pages        = {544--557},
  date         = {2009-08-27},
  doi          = {10.1016/j.neuron.2009.07.018},
  abstract     = {Neural circuits display complex activity patterns both
                  spontaneously and when responding to a stimulus or generating
                  a motor output. How are these two forms of activity related?
                  We develop a procedure called FORCE learning for modifying
                  synaptic strengths either external to or within a model neural
                  network to change chaotic spontaneous activity into a wide
                  variety of desired activity patterns. FORCE learning works
                  even though the networks we train are spontaneously chaotic
                  and we leave feedback loops intact and unclamped during
