                  served as a measure of the activity within a network.
                  Additionally, correlations of associated time courses served
                  as a measure of the connectivity between networks. To analyze
                  the temporal dynamics of between-network connectivity, we
                  computed the correlation matrices during sliding windows of 1
                  min and applied k-means clustering to the matrices during both
                  general anesthesia and wakefulness. RESULTS: Within-network
                  activity was decreased in the default mode, attentional, and
                  salience networks during general anesthesia (P < 0.001, range
                  of median changes: -0.34, -0.13). Average between-network
                  connectivity was reduced during general anesthesia (P < 0.001,
