                  brain activity. We demonstrate that loss of consciousness is
                  universally and reliably associated with stabilization of
                  cortical dynamics regardless of the specific activity
                  characteristics. To give an analogy, our analysis suggests
                  that loss of consciousness is akin to depressing the damper
                  pedal on the piano, which makes the sounds dissipate quicker
                  regardless of the specific melody being played. This approach
                  may prove useful in detecting consciousness on the basis of
                  brain activity under anesthesia and other settings.},
  note         = {- We argue that the brain, as a dynamical system, is
