  doi          = {10.1017/S0140525X1500031X},
  abstract     = {Memory is fleeting. New material rapidly obliterates previous
                  material. How, then, can the brain deal successfully with the
                  continual deluge of linguistic input? We argue that, to deal
                  with this "Now-or-Never" bottleneck, the brain must compress
