  doi          = {10.1038/ncomms11061},
  abstract     = {Flexible information routing fundamentally underlies the
                  function of many biological and artificial networks. Yet, how
                  such systems may specifically communicate and dynamically
                  route information is not well understood. Here we identify a
                  generic mechanism to route information on top of collective
                  dynamical reference states in complex networks. Switching
                  between collective dynamics induces flexible reorganization of
                  information sharing and routing patterns, as quantified by
