  abstract     = {We propose a theory of the early processing in the mammalian
                  visual pathway. The theory is formulated in the language of
                  information theory and hypothesizes that the goal of this
                  processing is to recode in order to reduce a “generalized
                  redundancy” subject to a constraint that specifies the amount
                  of average information preserved. In the limit of no noise,
                  this theory becomes equivalent to Barlow's redundancy
                  reduction hypothesis, but it leads to very different
