                  reaching consequences developing a better understanding of
                  consciousness promises to bring, for instance in diagnosing
                  disorders of consciousness (e.g., coma, vegetative-state,
                  locked-in syndrome), these theories are seldom tested via
                  invasive techniques (with high signal-to-noise ratios), and
                  never directly confronted within a single dataset. Here, we
                  first derive concrete and testable predictions from the global
                  neuronal workspace and integrated information theory of
                  consciousness. Then, we put these to the test by functionally
