  abstract     = {The winner-take-all (WTA) computation in networks of
                  recurrently connected neurons is an important decision element
                  of many models of cortical processing. However, analytical
                  studies of the WTA performance in recurrent networks have
                  generally addressed rate-based models. Very few have addressed
