  issue        = {11},
  pages        = {E2528--E2537},
  date         = {2018-03-13},
  doi          = {10.1073/pnas.1703643115},
  abstract     = {The mechanisms underlying analgesia related to social touch
                  are not clear. While recent research highlights the role of
                  the empathy of the observer to pain relief in the target, the
                  contribution of social interaction to analgesia is unknown.
                  The current study examines brain-to-brain coupling during pain
