                  conditions: either of two variants of the social connectedness
                  intervention or either of two control groups. Positivity
                  resonance, prosociality, and self-centeredness were measured
                  nightly for 35 consecutive days. Dynamic multilevel factor
                  models of nightly reports showed significant growth in
                  positivity resonance, relative to a passive control group, for
                  the two intervention groups and higher mean levels of
                  prosociality for one of them. In addition, significant
                  dose-response relations were evident (both between persons and
                  within persons), linking positivity resonance to both
                  prosociality and self-centeredness. The within-persons effect
