                  their retrieval from long-term memory to optimize attention in
                  search. Responses in ventrolateral and anterior thalamic
                  nuclei tracked learning of the predictiveness of these
                  abstract associations and their use in directing attention.
                  These findings demonstrate a key role for human thalamus in
                  higher-level cognition, notably, in mnemonic biasing of
