                  nonlinearity. This error can be fixed by adjusting the length
                  of the time series such that it becomes an integer multiple of
                  the dominant periodicity. The resulting time series will not
                  be a power of 2, and requires the use of a DFT to generate
                  surrogate data. DFT-based surrogates no longer detect spurious
                  nonlinearity, but cannot be used to detect periodic
                  nonlinearity. We propose a new test, nonlinear
                  cross-prediction (NLCP), which avoids some of the problems
                  associated with phase-randomised surrogate data, and which
                  allows reliable detection of both periodic and aperiodic
                  nonlinearity. In the test the original data are used to
                  construct a nonlinear model to predict the original data set
