  abstract     = {In this manuscript, we show that any neural network with any
                  activation function can be represented as a decision tree. The
                  representation is equivalence and not an approximation, thus
                  keeping the accuracy of the neural network exactly as is. We
                  believe that this work provides better understanding of neural
                  networks and paves the way to tackle their black-box nature.
