                  diversity. We also uncover selective correlations between
                  changes in signal diversity and phenomenological reports of
                  the intensity of psychedelic experience. This is the first
                  time that these measures have been applied to the psychedelic
                  state and, crucially, that they have yielded values exceeding
                  those of normal waking consciousness. These findings suggest
                  that the sustained occurrence of psychedelic phenomenology
