                  and engineering fields. For the linear version of this
                  problem, the so-called controllability Gramian has played an
                  important role to quantify how effectively the dynamical
                  states are reachable by a suitable driving input. In this
                  paper, we first extend the notion of the controllability
                  Gramian to nonlinear dynamics in terms of the Gibbs
