                  known, their relationship with statistical learning is largely
                  unexplored. We formalize a framework to learn the Koopman
                  operator from finite data trajectories of the dynamical
                  system. We consider the restriction of this operator to a
                  reproducing kernel Hilbert space and introduce a notion of
                  risk, from which different estimators naturally arise. We link
                  the risk with the estimation of the spectral decomposition of
