                  convection-diffusion equation in a multi-particle dynamic
                  system. In particular, how words in a sentence are abstracted
                  into contexts by passing through the layers of the Transformer
                  can be interpreted as approximating multiple particles'
                  movement in the space using the Lie-Trotter splitting scheme
                  and the Euler's method. Given this ODE's perspective, the rich
                  literature of numerical analysis can be brought to guide us in
                  designing effective structures beyond the Transformer. As an
                  example, we propose to replace the Lie-Trotter splitting
                  scheme by the Strang-Marchuk splitting scheme, a scheme that
                  is more commonly used and with much lower local truncation
                  errors. The Strang-Marchuk splitting scheme suggests that the
                  self-attention and position-wise feed-forward network (FFN)
                  sub-layers should not be treated equally. Instead, in each
                  layer, two position-wise FFN sub-layers should be used, and
                  the self-attention sub-layer is placed in between. This leads
                  to a brand new architecture. Such an FFN-attention-FFN layer
