                  (MBSR-ld) on indicators of stress in healthy working adults to
                  determine if results similar to those obtained in traditional
                  MBSR could be demonstrated. Participants were randomized into
                  MBSR-ld and wait-list control groups. Self-reported perceived
                  stress, sleep quality, and mindfulness were measured at the
                  beginning and end of the 6-week intervention. Salivary
                  cortisol was assessed weekly. Significant reductions in
                  perceived stress (p = .0025) and increases in mindfulness (p =
                  .0149) were obtained for only the MBSR-ld group (n = 22).
                  Scores on the global measure of sleep improved for the MBSR-ld
