                  canonical correlation to 3-way arrays (with dimensionality
                  number of signals by number of time points by number of
                  trials), 2) allows for nonstationarity, 3) also allows for
                  nonlinearity, 4) scales well as the number of signals
                  increases, and 5) captures predictive relationships, as is
                  done with Granger causality. We demonstrate the effectiveness
