                  unobserved variables can be recovered from the history of only
                  a handful of observed variables. To test whether language
                  models are effectively constructing delay embeddings, we
                  measure the capacities of sequence models to reconstruct
                  unobserved dynamics. We trained 1-layer transformer decoders
                  and state-space sequence models on next-step prediction from
