                  dimensional, mechanistic approach. We discuss the importance
                  that efforts to identify meaningful psychiatric dimensions be
                  coupled with careful computational modeling to formally
                  specify, test, and potentially falsify candidate mechanisms
                  that underlie transdiagnostic symptom dimensions. We refer to
                  this approach, i.e., where symptom dimensions are identified
                  and validated against computationally well-defined
                  neurocognitive processes, as computational factor modeling. We
                  describe in detail some recent applications of this method to
                  understand transdiagnostic cognitive processes that include
