  date         = {2024-07-27},
  doi          = {10.1038/s41398-024-03029-0},
  abstract     = {Ketamine is a dissociative anesthetic that induces a shift in
                  global consciousness states and related brain dynamics.
                  Portable low-density EEG systems could be used to monitor
                  these effects. However, previous evidence is almost null and
                  lacks adequate methods to address global dynamics with a small
                  number of electrodes. This study delves into brain high-order
                  interactions (HOI) to explore the effects of ketamine using
                  portable EEG. In a double-blinded cross-over design, 30 male
