                  -0.948). Effect sizes remained highly significant for
                  medication-free patients compared to controls across all
                  disorders. Smaller and significant reductions in HRV were
                  observed for specific antidepressants and antipsychotics.
                  LIMITATIONS: Study quality significantly moderated effect
                  sizes in case-control analyses, underscoring the importance of
