                over the unconstrained control-space and is therefore fast
                enough to allow real-time control of a full humanoid robot on
                modern computers. Although indirect methods automatically take
                into account state constraints, control limits pose a
                difficulty. This is particularly problematic when an expensive
                robot is strong enough to break itself. In this paper, we
