                  between PFC spikes and STR LFPs, but not the reverse,
                  reflecting the direct monosynaptic connections from the PFC to
                  STR. However, causal connectivity analyses suggested that the
                  polysynaptic connections from STR to the PFC exerted a
                  stronger overall influence. This supports models positing that
                  the basal ganglia "train" the PFC. Category learning may
                  depend on the formation of functional circuits between the PFC
                  and STR.},
