  doi          = {10.1103/PhysRevE.100.032305},
  abstract     = {This paper introduces a model-agnostic approach to study
                  statistical synergy, a form of emergence in which patterns at
                  large scales are not traceable from lower scales. Our
                  framework leverages various multivariate extensions of
                  Shannon's mutual information, and introduces the O-information
                  as a metric that is capable of characterizing synergy- and
                  redundancy-dominated systems. The O-information is a symmetric
                  quantity, and can assess intrinsic properties of a system
                  without dividing its parts into "predictors" and "targets." We
                  develop key analytical properties of the O-information, and
                  study how it relates to other metrics of high-order
                  interactions from the statistical mechanics and neuroscience
                  literature. Finally, as a proof of concept, we present an
