  date         = {2020-04-01},
  doi          = {10.1097/aln.0000000000003159},
  abstract     = {Abstract Background Ketamine is a noncompetitive
                  N-methyl-d-aspartate antagonist and is known for unique
                  electrophysiologic profiles in electroencephalography.
                  However, the mechanisms of ketamine-induced unconsciousness
                  are not clearly understood. The authors have investigated
                  neuronal dynamics of ketamine-induced loss and return of
