  date         = {1994-12-01},
  doi          = {10.1097/00000542-199412000-00029},
  abstract     = {BACKGROUND: The alpha 2-adrenergic agonists are members of a
                  novel class of hypnotic-anesthetic agents that selectively
                  bind to alpha 2 adrenoceptors in the locus coeruleus (LC) to
                  initiate their pharmacologic action. The postreceptor
                  molecular mechanism of the hypnotic action of alpha
